{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 70, :comments ["<b>And He chose</b> — For He had already chosen, in the manner of וישאל אותה and many like it, for Mount Zion David captured, and after his name Jerusalem is called, the city which David Hanun [?]." "<b>And He took him</b> — After He took him." "<b>From the sheepfolds</b> — Like: גזר ממכלה צאן (he cut off from the sheepfold)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "The phrase קרית חנה דוד is obscure; read hyper-literally. Possibly a corruption or reference to a city dedicated/named for David; the syntax and form of חנה are uncertain.", 1 "The comment is elliptical; Ibn Ezra apparently signals that ויקחהו refers to a taking subsequent to the choosing already mentioned."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:25.124758828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}